\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Analyst view during an interactive session. Above, attribution rows name the declared command of each side, one row marks the second agent's command as \texttt  {unaccounted}, and two \texttt  {scrub} records annotate the object deleted after the edge was published. Below, the agent's own reasoning is retained and labelled \texttt  {agent-authored}, so it is available to an analyst as context and can never be mistaken for evidence. Document counts are from the session shown, not from the evaluation runs in Section~4.}}{9}{figure.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:console}{{2}{9}{Analyst view during an interactive session. Above, attribution rows name the declared command of each side, one row marks the second agent's command as \texttt {unaccounted}, and two \texttt {scrub} records annotate the object deleted after the edge was published. Below, the agent's own reasoning is retained and labelled \texttt {agent-authored}, so it is available to an analyst as context and can never be mistaken for evidence. Document counts are from the session shown, not from the evaluation runs in Section~4}{figure.caption.30}{}}
